---
description: Navigation and loading rules that keep ModernLMS feeling like an SPA
globs: src/**/*.tsx
alwaysApply: false
---

# Never cause a full page reload

The entire pitch is "unlike Moodle, nothing reloads". A single full reload in the demo undoes it.

Bad:

```tsx
window.location.href = `/courses/${id}`;
<a href={`/courses/${id}`}>Open</a>
<form action="/api/assignments" method="post">
```

Good:

```tsx
const router = useRouter();
router.push(`/courses/${id}`);
<Link href={`/courses/${id}`} prefetch>Open</Link>
// mutations: fetch() or a server action, then router.refresh()
```

# Keep the shell out of the page

Sidebars, topbar, and the module tree belong in `layout.tsx`, never in `page.tsx`. If a sidebar
re-mounts on navigation it flickers, and the flicker is the thing we are selling against.

# Every route gets a skeleton

Add a `loading.tsx` next to each `page.tsx`. Skeletons match the real layout's shape so content
does not jump when it lands.

# Show retrieval before generation

In the ask flow, render citation cards as soon as retrieval returns and let the answer text fill
in above them. Do not block the whole result on the model call.
